# English code, Spanish replies

Code and names are English. Replies, explanations, and conversation with the user are Spanish.

This covers folders, files, packages, types, functions, variables, tests, scripts, comments, and error names. Progress updates, review notes, and chat answers stay in Spanish even when they quote English identifiers.

Product documents under `docs/` may stay in Spanish. Do not copy Spanish ubiquitous-language terms into identifiers.

```text
contexts/platform/domain/index.ts
shared/contracts
apps/api-cloud
apps/local-node
createApplication()
ApplicationModule
pnpm architecture
```

```text
contextos/plataforma
crearAplicacion()
ModuloAplicacion
pnpm arquitectura
```

- Test names use Given / When / Then.
- A new bounded context uses English layer names: `domain`, `application`, `adapters`.
- Rename an existing Spanish identifier when you touch that code. Do not add a Spanish alias beside the English name.
